"spell markdown" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;spell-markdown&gt;
		<header>Markdown drawn by spell's own engine, in ui-* elements.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A <link target="src-packages-ui-docs-ui-markdown-html" link="/components/ui/markdown"><text code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</></> drawn by spell's markdown engine instead of marked: headers, lists, tables, alerts and tasks as Spell UI's own elements, plain or <text code>editable</>. Its spell blocks are coloured by spell's parser.</>
	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone showing markdown with spell in it, or changing spell's markdown engine</>
		<item icon="play">Live: the real element, from the app's element build this page loads</>
	</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<example "1. Example" description="`editable`:  Write / Preview tabs, the preview drawn by spell's engine.">
			<html>
				<spell-markdown editable>
					<script type="text/markdown">
						# Try it

						Type **markdown** here, then look at the _Preview_.

						- [x] tables, task lists, alerts
						- [ ] your text

						> [!TIP]
						> Alerts become messages.

						```spell
						a pile is a list of cards
						```
					</script>
				</spell-markdown>
			</html>
		</example>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>Live, from <text code>/element/spell.pack.js</> (<text code>yarn build:element</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>), which this set's pages load.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Using it">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Everything <text code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</> takes: inline text or a <text code>source</> file, <text code>sanitized</> (which keeps its <text code>ui-*</> elements), <text code>heading-offset</>, <text code>skip-title</>, <text code>headings</> and <text code>reveal()</>.</>
			<item>Its engine is spell's (<text code>spell/parser/markdown</>, on the parser), a lazy chunk loaded with the first render.</>
			<item>It loads <text code>&lt;spell-code&gt;</> too, so a <text code>spell</> code block is coloured.</>
			<item>Compiled spell's own <text code>&lt;markdown&gt;</> blocks still draw with <text code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</>.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Attributes, events and texts">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<text paragraph>Its own names; the rest are <link target="src-packages-ui-docs-ui-markdown-html" link="/components/ui/markdown"><text code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</></>'s, which it extends:</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-api family="spell-markdown"></>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>From its vocabulary, by <text code>yarn site:data</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Its code">
		<icon slot="icon" name="folder open"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><link target="src-packages-app-components-spell-markdown-spellmarkdown-tsx" link="/src/app/components/spell-markdown/SpellMarkdown.tsx"><text title="src/app/components/spell-markdown/SpellMarkdown.tsx" code>SpellMarkdown.tsx</></>: its component, a <text code>UIMarkdown</> drawn by spell's engine</>
			<item><link target="src-packages-app-components-spell-markdown-spellmarkdown-en-ts" link="/src/app/components/spell-markdown/SpellMarkdown.en.ts"><text title="src/app/components/spell-markdown/SpellMarkdown.en.ts" code>SpellMarkdown.en.ts</></>: what its vocabulary adds to <text code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</>'s</>
			<item><link target="src-packages-app-components-spell-markdown-mdengine-ts" link="/src/app/components/spell-markdown/MDEngine.ts"><text title="src/app/components/spell-markdown/MDEngine.ts" code>MDEngine.ts</></>: spell's markdown engine, as <text code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</> asks for one</>
			<item>Its build: <text code>yarn build:element</>, into <text code>dist-element/</>, served at <text code>/element/</></>
		</>
	</>
